From 6cd043187e77d5ef53ab814f5d3633ab29ee8c6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:23:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 54/94] iio: common: qcom_smgr: fix the QMI layouts of the
 buffering messages

Read against the SMGR QMI IDL tables of the stock libsensor1.so
(SNS_SMGR_SVC v01):

- the notify-suspend TLV of a buffering request is a u32 proc_type and
  a u8 flag, not two u16s (never sent so far, it would have been
  malformed),
- TLV 2 of a buffering report is an array of at most 5 index entries
  {sensor_id, data_type, first_sample_idx, sample_count,
  first_sample_timestamp, sampling_rate}, not one metadata struct,
- a report sample is {data[3], u16 timestamp_offset, u8 flags,
  u8 quality}, and a report carries at most 100 of them,
- the largest message of the service is 0x68c bytes, the
  single-sensor-info response up to 0x419.

Decode reports per index entry: push every primary sample with its own
timestamp (the index timestamp plus the sum of the offsets, as the
stock HAL does) through a local scan buffer, and size the QMI receive
buffer for the largest message, so a report with more than one sample
is neither cut off nor overwritten by the IIO timestamp.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
